      content: 'PERSONIFICATION gives human qualities to non-human things: "the wind whispered", "opportunity knocked". METONYMY replaces a thing with something closely associated: "the Crown" (monarchy), "the White House said" (the US administration), "the pen is mightier than the sword" (writing vs force). SYNECDOCHE uses a part for the whole (or whole for part): "all hands on deck" (sailors), "nice wheels" (car).',
